# A plinko segment: a staggered pillar field with two shooters at the top of it,
# and one gentle climb so the run keeps rising.
#
# The stagger is the scatter. Pillar rows alternate between x 1,4,7,10,13 and
# x 2,5,8,11, so a ball never has a straight lane to fall down -- and column 6 is
# clear through the whole field, which is the lane a player can actually use.
#
# The shooters sit UP-BRIDGE of the field they feed, so their output travels back
# down at the party under the deck's own pitch. Authored at height 0 like every
# pool segment; the assembler stacks it.

name = run_pillars
base_height = 0
width = 21
length = 18
tags = plinko, pillars, ramp

